From 9aaf5f029916f95ed4c280ec5a9ec8e66e131ec5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 03:56:41 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Docker: run voice capture in a container

- Dockerfile: copy alembic.ini and alembic/ (the lifespan runs `alembic upgrade head`; the
  container crashed at start without them), put the venv on PATH for model-manager.sh, install
  the locked packages with CPU-only torch (5.5 GB instead of 15.2 GB; only silero-vad uses
  torch), strip CRLF from the shell scripts, run the server from the venv through
  deploy/docker-entrypoint.sh (seeds the chosen model if the volume lacks it; `uv run` would
  re-sync at every start), DATA_DIR=/data. The model layer sits before app/ so a code edit
  rebuilds in seconds.
- docker-compose.yml: pass CAPTURE_TOKEN, GEMINI_API_KEY, ANTHROPIC_API_KEY, CAPTURE_BACKEND,
  CAPTURE_MODEL, CAPTURE_TOPICS, CAPTURE_DEFAULT_CURRENCY, CAPTURE_TZ, ASK_BACKEND and
  CLAUDE_MODEL through; a whisper-data volume for DATA_DIR; a /status healthcheck; the port
  mapping is HOST:8000 (API_PORT was also used as the container port, which the server ignores).
- pyproject.toml, uv.lock: tzdata as a direct dependency (CAPTURE_TZ needs it on slim images and
  Windows).
- .dockerignore: models, data, evals, docs out of the build context.
- docs/CAPTURE-DOCKER.md: Windows and Linux steps, .env, iPhone reach, backup, speed.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
