index 0000000..986419e
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/CAPTURE-DOCKER.md
@@ -0,0 +1,142 @@
+# Voice capture in Docker
+
+Run the capture server in a container on an always-on machine (a Windows PC with Docker
+Desktop, or any Linux box). Read `docs/CAPTURE.md` first for what `/capture` does and for the
+iPhone Shortcut steps. This page covers only the container.
+
+Status of this page: every command below was run on Linux (Docker Engine 29, Compose v5,
+4-core x86 CPU, no GPU) unless it says **not run**. Nothing here was run on Windows or on a
+phone.
+
+## What you get
+
+- `docker compose up -d --build` builds one image (about 5.5 GB: Python and ffmpeg 0.7 GB,
+  libraries with CPU-only torch 1.3 GB, the `breeze-asr-25` speech model 1.6 GB) and starts it.
+- The speech model is downloaded while the image is built, so the first start needs no extra
+  step. If you later set `MODEL_NAME` to another model in the registry, the container fetches it
+  on start (`deploy/docker-entrypoint.sh`, about 20 s for `large-v3-turbo`).
+- Two named volumes survive `down`, `up` and `up --build`: `whisper-models` (`/app/models`) and
+  `whisper-data` (`/data`, which holds `capture/` and `history.db`).
+- Healthy when `GET /status` answers (the compose healthcheck calls it).
+
+## 1. Install Docker
+
+- **Windows:** install Docker Desktop with the WSL 2 backend. **Not run**: nothing on this page
+  was tried on Windows. Two risks to watch: Git may check files out with CRLF line endings (the
+  Dockerfile strips them from the shell scripts, **not run** with a real Windows checkout; it was
+  checked by converting the scripts to CRLF on Linux), and Docker Desktop keeps volumes inside its
+  VM, so use the backup command below, not Explorer.
+- **Linux:** install Docker Engine and the Compose plugin from Docker's repository, then
+  `sudo usermod -aG docker $USER` and log in again.
+
+## 2. Configure
+
+Get the code (the patched tree), then create `.env` next to `docker-compose.yml`.
+
+Linux or macOS:
+
+    cp .env.example .env        # then edit; or write the five lines below
+
+Windows PowerShell: `Copy-Item .env.example .env`
+
+Smallest useful `.env` (no spaces around `=`, no comment on the same line as a value):
+
+    CAPTURE_TOKEN=put-a-long-random-string-here
+    GEMINI_API_KEY=your-free-key-from-aistudio.google.com
+    CAPTURE_TZ=Asia/Kuala_Lumpur
+    CAPTURE_TOPICS=move: moving house,motorcycle: buying a bike
+    CAPTURE_DEFAULT_CURRENCY=MYR
+
+Make a token with `openssl rand -hex 24` or any password manager. Compose reads `.env` and the
+shell environment (the shell wins). These pass through to the container:
+
+| Variable | Default | Note |
+|---|---|---|
+| `CAPTURE_TOKEN` | empty | Empty: `/capture` answers 503 and refuses everything. |
+| `GEMINI_API_KEY` | empty | Free tier sorts the notes (15 requests a minute). |
+| `ANTHROPIC_API_KEY` | empty | If set, `CAPTURE_BACKEND=auto` sorts with Claude. |
+| `CAPTURE_BACKEND` | `auto` | `claude`, `gemini` or `auto`. |
+| `CAPTURE_MODEL` | empty | Empty uses the code default for the backend. |
+| `CAPTURE_TOPICS` | empty | Comma separated `slug: description`. |
+| `CAPTURE_DEFAULT_CURRENCY` | `MYR` | |
+| `CAPTURE_TZ` | empty (container is UTC) | Set it: files are stamped in this zone (`+08:00`). |
+| `ASK_BACKEND` | `gemini` | `claude` makes the unauthenticated `/ask` spend your Claude key. |
+| `CLAUDE_MODEL` | empty | |
+| `MODEL_NAME` | `breeze-asr-25` | Any key in `registry/models.yaml`. |
+| `API_PORT` | `8000` | The host port. The server always listens on 8000 inside. |
+
+`GEMINI_MODEL` defaults to `gemini-2.5-flash` in `docker-compose.yml` (as shipped upstream), but
+the code default in `app/services/llm.py` is `gemini-3.1-flash-lite`. It only changes `/ask`;
+`/capture` uses `CAPTURE_MODEL` or its own default. Set `GEMINI_MODEL` in `.env` to match if you
+care.
+
+## 3. Start
+
+    docker compose up -d --build
+    docker compose ps            # wait for "healthy"
+    curl http://localhost:8000/status
+
+Measured on the Linux box: cold build 130 s (base images already pulled; apt, Python packages and
+the model downloaded fresh), time to healthy 20 s after `up`, idle memory about 1.8 GiB
+(`docker stats`). The first Windows build will also have to pull the base images.
+
+Image size: 5.47 GB. The lockfile resolves torch to the CUDA build, and the same tree built with
+the lockfile's wheels is much larger (see below); the Dockerfile swaps in the CPU wheels
+(`TORCH_INDEX`, only silero-vad uses torch). `COMPUTE_TYPE` and `DEVICE=auto` run on the CPU.
+With CPU torch the silero VAD loads (`/status` reports `"vad": {"backend": "silero"}`) and the
+capture tests pass inside the container (76 passed). For a GPU container set `TORCH_INDEX=` in
+`.env` and add the GPU runtime to the compose file yourself: **not run**.
+
+## 4. Check it
+
+    curl -s -o /dev/null -w "%{http_code}\n" -X POST localhost:8000/capture \
+      -H 'Content-Type: application/json' -d '{"text":"x"}'        # 401, no token
+    curl -s -X POST localhost:8000/capture -H "Authorization: Bearer $CAPTURE_TOKEN" \
+      -H 'Content-Type: application/json' \
+      -d '{"text": "paid 500 ringgit deposit for the bike, collect it Saturday"}'
+
+A wrong token is also 401; an empty `CAPTURE_TOKEN` in `.env` is 503. The text call above came back
+sorted into an expense (500 MYR) and a task due the next Saturday, and the files appeared in the
+volume.
+
+## 5. Reach it from the iPhone
+
+- **Same Wi-Fi (LAN):** find the PC's address (`ipconfig` on Windows, `ip addr` on Linux) and use
+  `http://<that-address>:8000`. On Windows allow the Docker Desktop prompt through the firewall.
+  **Not run** (no phone, no Windows).
+- **Away from home (Tailscale):** install Tailscale on the PC and the phone, then use
+  `http://<pc-name>.<tailnet>.ts.net:8000`. **Not run.**
+- **The Shortcut works over plain HTTP** (the Get Contents of URL action posts the audio with the
+  Bearer header). This is the setup in `docs/CAPTURE.md`; **not run on a phone**.
+- **The page's Record button needs HTTPS.** Browsers allow the microphone only on HTTPS or
+  `localhost`. Put HTTPS in front with Tailscale (`docs/HTTPS-TAILSCALE.md`), then open
+  `https://<pc-name>.<tailnet>.ts.net/capture/ui`. The item list and tick boxes work over HTTP;
+  only Record does not. **Not run.**
+- Do not expose port 8000 to the internet. `/transcribe`, `/ask` and `/listen` have no token.
+
+## 6. Your data, and backups
+
+Captures live in the `whisper-data` volume under `capture/`: `tasks.md`, `notes.md`,
+`expenses.csv` (`notes.md` appears with the first note; `transcripts.jsonl` and `inbox.md` too). They survive `docker compose down` and
+`up --build` (checked: after `down`, `up` and a rebuild after a source edit, the item list still
+held the earlier task and both expenses). `docker compose down -v` deletes them.
+
+Back up from the running container (works on Windows too):
+
+    docker compose cp whisper-wrap:/data/capture ./capture-backup
+
+Copy `capture-backup` somewhere safe on a schedule. To restore into a fresh volume, start the
+container once and run `docker compose cp ./capture-backup/. whisper-wrap:/data/capture/`.
+
+## 7. Speed
+
+Seconds per note on a 4-core CPU with no GPU (`breeze-asr-25`, short clips of 2 to 8 seconds):
+about 12 s in the server, 13.5 s for a whole `/capture` call from a clip through sorting. Longer
+notes take longer. `large-v3-turbo` is slower here (about 15.6 s). A Windows PC will differ:
+**not run**.
+
+## 8. Update, stop, remove
+
+    docker compose up -d --build     # after pulling new code; data and models stay
+    docker compose down              # stop; volumes stay
+    docker compose down -v           # also deletes models and ALL captured data
